# plans/plan_dx9.md D9-A5 scene corpus: colored_trianglestrip_quad
# Every scene in this corpus so far uses primitive=TriangleList (grep-verified: it's the ONLY
# PrimitiveType value any .scene file has ever set), even though the scene format has supported
# TriangleStrip/LineList/LineStrip since D9-A3's own original design (Oracle.cs's PrimitiveVerts()
# already handles all 4) and CNA's own D3D9EffectDraw.cpp/DirectX9Renderer.cpp already have a
# real, non-stub PrimitiveType->D3DPT_* mapping (ToD3D9Topology(), used unconditionally by every
# draw call this whole corpus issues) -- but the TriangleStrip-specific vertex-count/
# primitive-count conversion chain (GraphicsDevice::PrimitiveVerts(), the inverse of
# DrawUserPrimitives's own primitiveCount->vertexCount expansion) and D3DPT_TRIANGLESTRIP itself
# have never been exercised end to end against the real XNA oracle. A genuine, previously-untested
# gap, not a new feature -- no code changes needed on either side, matching this session's
# "reuse existing infrastructure" scenes.
#
# A 4-vertex colored quad in the canonical "Z" strip order (TL,TR,BL,BR) -- the standard pattern
# that keeps both resulting triangles consistently front-facing under a strip's automatic
# alternating-winding rule, so neither gets back-face culled by XNA's default
# RasterizerState.CullCounterClockwise. Four DIFFERENT corner colors (not a single flat color)
# specifically so a broken triangle-count/vertex-count computation (e.g. off-by-one, dropping the
# second triangle, or misinterpreting the 4 vertices as a single degenerate triangle) is
# immediately visible as a missing quadrant or wrong Gouraud gradient, not just "did it crash".
width=256
height=256
profile=HiDef
clearcolor=100,149,237,255
vertexcolor=true
lighting=false
primitive=TriangleStrip
vertex=-0.6,0.6,0,255,0,0,255
vertex=0.6,0.6,0,0,255,0,255
vertex=-0.6,-0.6,0,0,0,255,255
vertex=0.6,-0.6,0,255,255,0,255
